M4.2 — async compaction worker (completing the M4.2 task surface)
===================================================================
Node: M4.2 (Compaction epochs + async worker + stale rejection + sync
fallback)
Phase context: Future-tasks Phase 2 exit work (between-nights M4 program)
Revision: commit "M4.2: async compaction worker — off-thread plans with a
bounded arrival window" on main
Environment: macOS darwin 25.5.0 arm64, local dev profile, UTC

WHAT CHANGED
------------
Epochs, stale rejection (apply_compaction Stale) and the synchronous
fallback were delivered with Phase 2.2 (E2E-proven on M2.7: the
daemon_compaction_e2e hot-path proof). The ASYNC WORKER did not exist
anywhere; this commit completes the task's named surface (docs/19
"async compaction result ... accepted only if the source branch/
generation is still current ... hard pressure before async result
arrives -> bounded synchronous compaction"):

- at each turn boundary, when the conversation estimate passes a soft
  threshold (budget/5), a worker thread precomputes the compaction
  plan off the turn thread and signals a Condvar
- a boundary that finds the conversation over budget gives a pending
  worker a bounded 5ms arrival window; a late plan falls back to the
  synchronous path (the Phase 2.2 behavior, unchanged)
- freshness: plans are INDEX-BASED (truncate at i / summarize [s,e)),
  so appended messages (new turns, steer notes) do not shift them — a
  precomputed plan goes stale only on a structural change (a compaction
  apply bumps the structure epoch); stale plans are discarded and
  recomputed
- the scheduler enables the worker on the production path

